-- Node: lp-paramedian-start (3 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":5,"title":"Paramedian Approach — Technique","body":"**Why paramedian?** [2][12][16]\n• Midline route crosses the supraspinous and interspinous ligaments, which are frequently ossified, with osteophytes, in elderly patients and those with spine pathology\n• Paramedian route passes through paraspinal soft tissue and reaches the interlaminar window lateral to those ligaments\n• **30-40% higher first-attempt success** than midline in trial data [12]\n• Does not require full spinal flexion; works in lateral decubitus or sitting\n• L5-S1 is usually the largest interlaminar space and often the most accessible in older patients [16]\n\n**Best for:**\n• Age >50 or known degenerative spine disease\n• Failed midline attempts\n• Kyphosis or scoliosis\n• Limited ability to flex\n\n**Use caution:** severe obesity (longer, less predictable path).\n\n**Layers traversed (paramedian):**\n1. Skin\n2. Subcutaneous tissue\n3. Paraspinal muscles\n4. Ligamentum flavum\n5. Epidural space\n6. Dura mater\n7. Subarachnoid space\n\n**Needle feel differs from midline:** there is no ligamentous loss of resistance. Often the only distinct give is the dural puncture. [16]","citation":[2,12,16],"next":"lp-paramedian-insertion","summary":"Paramedian: target L4-L5 or L5-S1; enter 2 cm lateral and 2 cm caudal; aim 30-45° cephalomedial","skippable":true}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'lp-paramedian-start' AND tree_id = 'lumbar-puncture';

-- Node: lp-paramedian-steps (4 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":5,"title":"Paramedian LP — Step-by-Step Guide","body":"[Why and when](#/node/lp-paramedian-start) | [Insertion detail and troubleshooting](#/node/lp-paramedian-insertion)\n\n**Technique per Hadzic (NYSORA).** [16]\n\n---\n\n**STEP 1: LOCATE THE TARGET INTERSPACE**\n• Straighten the patient first; correct any lean if scoliosis is present\n• Keep one hand on the **iliac crest** and your thumb on the **midline spinous processes** throughout\n• Intercristal (Tuffier) line crosses at about **L4-L5** in most, not all, patients\n• Whatever palpation suggests, stay in the **lower third of the lumbar spine**: target **L4-L5 or L5-S1**. L5-S1 is usually the largest interlaminar space\n\n---\n\n**STEP 2: MARK THE ENTRY POINT**\nFrom the center of the target interspace:\n• **2 cm lateral** to midline\n• **2 cm caudal**\n• Infiltrate local anesthetic into skin, subcutaneous tissue and paraspinal muscle along the planned track\n\n---\n\n**STEP 3: TRAJECTORY AND CONFIRMATION**\n• Direct the needle **30-45° cephalad and medially**, toward the interspace\n• **Expect no ligamentous loss of resistance.** The needle crosses soft tissue only; the first distinct give is usually the dura\n• Advance in small steps and check the hub for CSF frequently\n• Bone (lamina): withdraw to subcutaneous tissue, redirect more cephalad and walk off the superior lamina edge","citation":[12,16],"next":"lp-paramedian-insertion","images":[{"src":"images/lumbar-puncture/lp-paramedian-step1-locate.jpg","alt":"Step 1 — Locate the L5-S1 interspace by palpating iliac crests","caption":"Step 1: Hand on the iliac crest, thumb on the midline. The intercristal line crosses near L4-L5; stay in the lower lumbar spine (L4-L5 or L5-S1)."},{"src":"images/lumbar-puncture/lp-paramedian-step2-entry.jpg","alt":"Step 2 — Mark entry point 2 cm lateral and 2 cm caudal from L5-S1","caption":"Step 2: Entry point 2 cm lateral to midline and 2 cm caudal to the center of the target interspace."},{"src":"images/lumbar-puncture/lp-paramedian-step3-trajectory.jpg","alt":"Step 3 — Trajectory 30-45 degrees cephalad and toward midline","caption":"Step 3: Trajectory 30-45° cephalad and medial. Soft tissue only; the first distinct give is usually the dura. Technique per Dr. Hadzic (NYSORA)."}],"summary":"Paramedian 3-step: L4-L5 or L5-S1 → entry 2 cm lateral + 2 cm caudal → 30-45° cephalomedial, no ligament LOR","skippable":true}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'lp-paramedian-steps' AND tree_id = 'lumbar-puncture';

-- Node: lp-paramedian-insertion (2 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":5,"title":"Paramedian — Needle Insertion","body":"**Entry point:** [16]\n• **2 cm lateral and 2 cm caudal** to the center of the target interspace (L4-L5 or L5-S1)\n• Iliac crest hand and midline thumb stay on the landmarks until the needle is placed\n\n**Needle trajectory:**\n1. Introduce through the anesthetized skin wheal\n2. Angle **30-45° cephalad and medially**, toward the interlaminar window\n3. The track crosses paraspinal muscle, then ligamentum flavum, then dura\n\n**Depth:** typically 4-8 cm; the oblique track is longer than midline\n\n**Tactile feedback:**\n• No supraspinous or interspinous ligament pops\n• Ligamentum flavum is often subtle; the **dural puncture may be the only distinct loss of resistance** [16]\n• Withdraw the stylet frequently once near expected depth\n\n**If bone (lamina) is contacted:**\n• Note depth (lamina sits just superficial to the interlaminar window)\n• Withdraw to subcutaneous tissue\n• Redirect more cephalad and walk off the superior edge of the lamina\n• If repeated contact, adjust the medial angle; consider ultrasound to mark the interlaminar window\n\n**Opening pressure:** measure in lateral decubitus with legs extended after CSF return.","citation":[2,12,16],"next":"lp-csf-obtained","summary":"Paramedian avoids supraspinous and interspinous ligaments — useful in elderly with calcification","skippable":true}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'lp-paramedian-insertion' AND tree_id = 'lumbar-puncture';

